static assertion failed
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/7: the instantiation of a pack expansion over an EMPTY
pack produces an empty list.  An empty type pack is recorded in the
template map's pack sizes only, and the drain that expands pack expansions
in function bodies ran only for value packs or type packs of two or more
elements, so `{1, f<Ts>()...}' with no Ts kept its pattern, instantiated
once with the empty pack's placeholder type (`f<void>()'): an array of two
elements instead of one.  The eager conversion of a constexpr / deduced-
return-type function (convert_function) had the same gap -- libc++'s
`constexpr _CCC __type_kinds[] = {_StrongOrd, __type_to_enum<_Ts>()...}'
in __get_comp_type for common_comparison_category_t<> (KNOWNBUG
cpp20_compare_three_way_pointers_libcxx).  Fixed in round 163b.
